# Patch1 quotes lines 1-20 of f whole, adds ADDED after FF, and changes L20 to
# P1_L20. Patch2 is numbered three lines lower and quotes three separate windows
# of the same file, skipping GAP1 and GAP2: it changes L06 to P2_L06, adds the
# same ADDED after FF, and changes L19 to P2_L19, and it quotes DIFF1_V2 and
# DIFF2_V2 where patch1 quotes DIFF1 and DIFF2. The report must show the L06,
# L19, and L20 changes on their own patch's side and leave out the shared ADDED
# line. The context section must show L06, DIFF1, and DIFF2 against patch2's
# lines, split at the gap so that the second part numbers FD by each patch's own
# line (11 and 8), and it must not show GAP1 or GAP2, which patch2 never quotes,
# as differences.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
exit: 0
